 "contract": {
  "mutable": [
   "skin"
  ],
  "preserve": [
   "motion"
  ],
  "notes": "A lamp and what it fails to reach: each shadow is thrown softer and shallower the further it falls, which is the whole idea and is carried by the falloff terms rather than by any colour. The palette is a five-stop ramp from a near-black ground to a near-white core \u2014 that RANGE is load-bearing. Tint it, but keep the ground dark and the top stop bright, or the core stops reading as a source and the field goes flat grey. It is the darkest asset of the three and the one to reach for behind light type; do not try to invert it into a light background by swapping the ends of the ramp, which produces a photographic negative rather than a lit room."
 }
